{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "1TH",
  "chapter": 1,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "1TH.1.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TH.1.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Paul, and Silvanus, and Timothy, to the church of the Thessalonians ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in God the Father, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the Lord Jesus Christ: Grace ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to you, and peace, from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "1TH.1.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TH.1.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "We give thanks to God always for you all, making mention of you in our prayers;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TH.1.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TH.1.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Remembering without ceasing your work of faith, and labor of love, and patience of hope in our Lord Jesus Christ, in the sight of God and our Father;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TH.1.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TH.1.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Knowing, brethren beloved by God, your election.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TH.1.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TH.1.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For our gospel came not to you in word only, but also in power, and in the Holy Spirit, and in much assurance; as ye know what manner of men we were among you for your sake.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TH.1.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TH.1.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And ye became followers of us, and of the Lord, having received the word in much affliction, with joy of the Holy Spirit:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TH.1.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TH.1.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So that ye were examples to all that believe, in Macedonia and Achaia.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TH.1.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TH.1.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For from you sounded out the word of the Lord not only in Macedonia and Achaia, but also in every place your faith toward God is spread abroad; so that we need not to speak any thing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TH.1.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TH.1.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For they themselves show of us what manner of entrance we had to you, and how ye turned to God from idols, to serve the living and true God;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TH.1.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TH.1.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And to wait for his Son from heaven, whom he raised from the dead, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Jesus, who delivered us from the wrath to come.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
